@startuml
title SplitSmart - Expense Submission and Approval
start
:Collect amount, date, description, split, participants and optional receipt;
:Call SubmitExpenseUseCase;
:Load group and validate submitter membership;
:Validate amount > 0;
:Validate submitterUserId == payerUserId and payer is a participant;
:Validate split and calculate BigDecimal shares;
if (Submission valid?) then (yes)
  :Persist expense as PENDING_REVIEW;
  :Request notification to other group members;
  :Show pending status;
  :Reviewer submits decision;
  :Load pending expense;
  if (Reviewer authorized under configured policy?) then (yes)
    :Record authorized ApprovalEvent;
    if (Decision is APPROVE?) then (yes)
      :Apply configured approval policy;
      if (All required approvals recorded?) then (yes)
        :Set expense APPROVED;
        :Persist expense and approval events;
        :Recalculate balances from approved expenses and payments;
        :Show updated balances;
      else (no)
        :Keep expense out of balances;
        :Await remaining required approval(s);
      endif
    else (no)
      if (Decision is REJECT?) then (yes)
        :Record REJECT decision;
        :Keep expense out of balances;
        :Apply rejection transition policy [UNRESOLVED];
      else (REQUEST_CHANGES)
        :Record REQUEST_CHANGES decision;
        :Keep expense out of balances;
        :Apply change/resubmission policy [UNRESOLVED];
      endif
    endif
  else (no)
    :Return unauthorized reviewer response;
    :Expense remains excluded from balances;
    :Unauthorized-action audit policy [UNRESOLVED];
  endif
else (no)
  :Return validation errors;
  :Do not submit expense;
endif
stop

note right
  Confirmed: pending expenses do not affect balances;
  an expense becomes eligible only after all configured
  approvals are recorded. The detailed specification
  permits one or multiple approvals.

  Unresolved: reviewer permissions, self-approval,
  reviewer selection/order, rejection transition, and
  REQUEST_CHANGES state/resubmission. These branches
  identify policy points without choosing their outcomes.
end note
@enduml
